hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2784","Narrated to us Yunus ibn 'Abd al-A'la, who said: Narrated to us Ibn Wahb, who said: Malik informed him.

And narrated to us al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub, who said: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, who said: Narrated to us Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah (RA), that she said:
""We went out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and we entered into the state of ihram for 'umrah. Those who had entered into ihram for 'umrah performed tawaf of the House and [performed] sa'i between as-Safa and al-Marwah, then they exited the state of ihram.""

**CHAPTER:**"
"2785","###
 Narrated to us Muhammad bin Al-Waleed Al-Qurashi, who said: Narrated to us Abdul-Wahhab, meaning Al-Thaqafi, who said: Narrated to us Habib, who is Al-Mu'allim, who said: 'Ata' narrated to me, saying: Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) reported that the Prophet (ﷺ) commanded his companions to make their Hajj an Umrah, then to perform Tawaf, then to shorten their hair or shave it, except for those who had with them"
